## Reviewer points not applied as stated

1. es-a #27. Q16–Q20 are body blocks because that is the Korean source shape, not because Spanish failed to promote them to headings. Adding ## or deleting the U+200B lines fails the checker. The first-person register was fixed inside the blocks.
2. es-a #36. The English source has a Difficulty row (Easy / Difficult / Easy). Deleting it drops that comparison and a table row. The bare «Sencillo» was the real problem; the cells now say «Dificultad del trámite | Menor | Mayor | Menor».
3. es-b #8. «hasta un importe igual» alone deletes the statutory «one time», which the checker counts as 1. The sentence keeps «una vez» and then says that is an amount equal to the actual damage.
4. es-a #39. «por cada año completo» with no word for 1 fails numbers. «un año» / «por cada un año completo» is the form the checker accepts.
5. es-a #3 suggested dropping the gloss 分支機構. It is kept, moved onto «sucursal», so the Traditional-Chinese gloss stays and is no longer attached to «oficina local».
6. Not every «juntos» is the calque. The ones that mean people or issues physically or procedurally together were left (listed above).
